Z||000000||JohnnyK||12-18-2000||09:02 AM||||I got a question about nitrous. How does it work? I mean, I know how it works, but this bugs me. If you are in neutral, and you give it a shot, will it rev real high? Also, say your just cruising along at a steady speed and give it a shot, will it rev and increase speed? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||10:29 AM||||it ONLY comes on  (ok if wire CORRECTLY) it ONLY comes on at WIDE OPEN THROTTLE! so you can leave it "Armed" all day for weeks on end and never have a problem.. HOWEVER.. your solenoids CAN/WILL fail so it's recommended you close the bottle or "disarm" the system and use what is left in the lines before you just walk away from the car.. if you blow nitrous into the engine while at idle, your rpms WILL go up and the engine will lean out and you'll blow the intake off the car! TOTALLY off the car! Engineered has fix a couple cars cause of this.. cause a person put the activation switch where they can actually reach it. and hit the button at part throttle in a parking lot and BOOOOOOOM!!! dead car.. holes in hood, blown tires! bad thing happen to the family! follow the provided instructions and have the included activation switch hooked to the fuel pressure switch and only to be activated at WOT. the Venom VCN-2000 no matter what they put in their lierature and no matter what your buddy told you is just like every other nitrous kit only activated at WOT.. (we've delt with Venom/Python remanufacturers on 5-6 NOPI show cars) the ONLY part throttle chatter box you can by that is worth a damn is the NOS Progressive Nitrous Controller from NOS. ($585) and worth EVERY penny! but who races at part throttle anyway.. if your gunna pick a fight, don't just pester;  DOMINATE!  I went through 16+ bottles in 6 months and NEVER had a nitrous related problem... I DID however kill clutches left and right... but the solid hub thats in it now i NEVER had a problem with... if you have an auto tranny thats another game.. for more info on nitrous and autos get a hold of Shaun41178@aol.com he's a fellow forum member with an 85 GT auto with nitrous. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>   my street driving numbers... not bad for a car with 96,000 miles on it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||count_iblis||12-18-2000||11:43 AM||||Ok here is a question.  I want to get around 75+ hp out of my fiero. I just got the car back from a engine swap.  2.8-3.1  Now Im going to do Nitrous due to it being the cheapest way to get where I want for now.  How bad is this going to screw my engine up?  I have the slightest clue as to anything about this. What would be the best kit and what is the  safest  H.P. squeeze considered?  I hope I said that right.  How much H.P is enogh before killing my fiero.  Im tired of my frineds V-tec and these damn redneck  Mustang owners ( I live in a small hick town).<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||count_iblis||12-18-2000||11:52 AM||||Also once the bottle runs out where do you go to get it refilled?  You just cant go to your local 7-11 and get it refilled.  Can you? <P>Chris<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||12:04 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.nosnitrous.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nosnitrous.com</A>  part #05120 or <A HREF="http://www.nitrousworks.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrousworks.com</A>  #13093 these are adjustable kits that start at 70hp but only about 40lbft at the wheels.  at <A HREF="http://www.nosnitrous.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nosnitrous.com</A>  they have a listing of refilling stations... if they don't have one listed near you call pye-baker welding supply or any welding supply or medical supply company they will be able to direct you to the nearest refilling station. with the stock jetting, premium fuel and fuel delivery system working properly you shouldn't ever have a problem. i didn't... the problems i had were self inflicked... (clutchs, brakes, motor mounts) all from shifitng to hard with a solid clutch, braking to hard warping rotors and motor mounts from the torque and braking they would self destruct in a month and rattle your eyeballs! ||||reg||1
